From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 20:45:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] art: riscv64 JIT emits no Zba/Zbb without the extensions

Riscv64Assembler gains ShiftAdd, MinS, MaxS, RotateLeft, RotateRight and RotateRightImm: the Zba/Zbb instruction when the extension is enabled, a base-ISA sequence otherwise. The code generator and intrinsics use them; the riscv64 simplifier makes ShiftAdd/BitwiseNegatedRight nodes only with Zba/Zbb; intrinsics built on Zbb (bit count, clz/ctz, reverse, reverse bytes, String.compareTo, byte-array views) stay unimplemented without it, as x86-64 does for popcnt. With the extensions enabled the emitted code is unchanged.

Licence of the patched files: Apache-2.0 (their AOSP headers).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AOSP targets rv64gcv_zba_zbb_zbs]
Patch-Reason: a riscv64 host target is plain rv64gc, where the JIT reads its features from the build (no Zba/Zbb) yet emitted them unconditionally (SIGILL); the instruction choice is inside the code generator, nothing outside the source can change it
---
